.TH SEARCH 1 "September 2026" "ProwseTk" "Prowse-TUI Help"
.SH NAME
search \- regex search within and across help pages
.SH LOCAL SEARCH
Press / in the help pager to open the search prompt. Enter a POSIX extended
regular expression and press Enter. Esc cancels the prompt without changing
the previous search. n advances to the next matching line and ? goes backwards.
Both directions wrap. One result is recorded per matching line.
An invalid regex leaves the prior search and cursor intact.
An expression with no matches reports zero matches and clears highlights.
.SH GLOBAL SEARCH
.B :help find navigation|plugin
Search the text of all help pages, including headings and link labels.
The result list is navigable with j/k or Up/Down. Enter opens the selected page
at the matching line. h goes back to the results. / also searches this index.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
:help find Lua|native
:help open commands
/endpoint.*discovery
n
?
.fi
.SH LIMITS
Patterns contain at most 1024 bytes. Help pages are at most 256 KiB;
there are at most 128 pages and 20000 displayed results.
Searching is case-sensitive and line-based; resize reflows the searchable text.
